From 2fa1f6156fd42e6cd64930387f2480657c77ffb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:56:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Offer a jump to a first letter in every library listing

Scrolling is currently the only way through a library listing, which pages 50
items at a time - reaching T in a few thousand artists means dozens of loads,
and the search box matches anywhere in a name so it cannot stand in for one.

Every library view gains a toolbar entry listing A-Z plus '#' for the items
filed under no letter, so the whole alphabet is one click away and the buckets
between them reach every item. Choosing the letter already showing clears it,
like the other toggle filters.

The letter is sent to the server, which files items by whichever name the
current sort uses - so the letters keep agreeing with the order on screen when
you switch between name and sort name.

The count endpoints take no letter, so a letter-filtered listing reports no
total rather than the whole library's, the same way a provider-filtered one
already does. Checked before the cached store count, which would otherwise be
returned for a narrowed list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VpS6zTXcRdworxLZ6Dp1De
